  "body": "### What is the issue with the URL Pattern Standard?\n\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/urlpattern/commit/46c30fda8f98edeeb6aeb252243a9ba67894f4bf causes a significant number of WPT tests to begin failing. In my implementation, this causes 219 tests to begin failing for `urlpattern/urlpattern.any.html` (from 8 to 227).\n\nAs an example, the input value of: `/foo` in \"canonicalize a pathname\" now produces the canonicalization of `//foo` instead of the expected `/foo`.\n\nI believe this is because the new dummy URL now has a path list containing the empty string (previously the empty list), which the URL parser is now appending to.\n\nI.e, the path segments of the resulting URL change from the list << `foo` >> to the list << `\"\"`, `foo` >>\n\nAfter adding an extra step between creating the dummy URL and running the basic URL parser to set the URL paths to the empty list, the regression is fixed, and in combination with 46c30fda causes 5 new tests to begin passing.\n\ncc @annevk  @sisidovski ",
